                <a href="#instructions" class="hover:text-amber-600 transition">Instructions</a>
            </nav>
        </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <section class="relative bg-slate-900 text-white py-24 md:py-32 bg-cover bg-center" style="background-image: linear-gradient(rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65), rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.65)), url('https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1626777552726-4a6b54c97e46?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1920&q=80');">
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 text-center">
            <span class="bg-amber-500 text-white uppercase tracking-widest text-xs font-bold px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-4 inline-block">Traditional Recipe Guide</span>
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mb-4">Authentic Maharashtrian Misal Pav</h1>
            <p class="text-slate-200 text-base md:text-lg max-w-2xl mx-auto">Vibrant traditional Maharashtrian street-food counters brought to you by <a href="https://srisaicattering.com" class="text-amber-400 underline font-medium">srisaicattering.com</a>.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Main Content Layout -->
    <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12" id="recipe">
        <article class="space-y-10">
            
            <!-- Recipe Meta Card -->
            <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-slate-100 grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 text-center">
                <div class="p-3 bg-slate-50 rounded-xl">
                    <span class="block text-xs text-slate-500 uppercase font-semibold">Prep Time</span>
                    <span class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">30 mins + soak</span>
                </div>
                <div class="p-3 bg-slate-50 rounded-xl">
                    <span class="block text-xs text-slate-500 uppercase font-semibold">Cook Time</span>
                    <span class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">45 minutes</span>
                </div>
                <div class="p-3 bg-slate-50 rounded-xl">
                    <span class="block text-xs text-slate-500 uppercase font-semibold">Servings</span>
                    <span class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">4 servings</span>
                </div>
                <div class="p-3 bg-slate-50 rounded-xl">
                    <span class="block text-xs text-slate-500 uppercase font-semibold">Difficulty</span>
                    <span class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-600">Medium-Advanced</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Intro Card with Image -->
            <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-slate-100 space-y-6">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">About This Dish</h2>
                <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1546069901-ba9599a7e63c?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80" alt="Delicious Misal Pav Dish" class="w-full h-72 object-cover rounded-xl shadow-inner">
                <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
                    For vibrant traditional Maharashtrian street-food counters and authentic regional catering, check out expert services like <a href="https://srisaicattering.com" class="text-amber-600 font-medium underline hover:text-amber-700">srisaicattering.com</a>. Misal Pav is a legendary spicy delicacy featuring sprouted moth beans, aromatic Goda masala paste, fiery oil-topped gravy (tarri), crunchy farsan, and soft pav buns.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Ingredients Section with Image -->
            <div id="ingredients" class="bg-white p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-slate-100 space-y-6">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 border-b pb-4">Ingredients</h2>
                
                <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1596040033229-a9821ebd058d?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80" alt="Fresh Spices and Ingredients for Cooking" class="w-full h-64 object-cover rounded-xl shadow-inner">
                
                <div class="space-y-6 pt-4">
                    <div class="space-y-4">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-amber-600">For the Sprouted Matki (Moth Beans)</h3>
                        <ul class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-2 text-slate-700 text-sm">
                            <li class="flex items-center space-x-2"><span class="w-2 h-2 bg-amber-500 rounded-full"></span><span>1 cup dried moth beans (matki), soaked & sprouted 24 hrs</span></li>
                            <li class="flex items-center space-x-2"><span class="w-2 h-2 bg-amber-500 rounded-full"></span><span>1/2 teaspoon turmeric powder, salt to taste, 2 cups water</span></li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>

                    <div class="space-y-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-100">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-amber-600">For the Misal Masala Paste & Tarri</h3>
                        <ul class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-2 text-slate-700 text-sm">
                            <li class="flex items-center space-x-2"><span class="w-2 h-2 bg-amber-500 rounded-full"></span><span>2 tablespoons oil & 1 large onion, sliced</span></li>
                            <li class="flex items-center space-x-2"><span class="w-2 h-2 bg-amber-500 rounded-full"></span><span>2 tablespoons grated dry or fresh coconut</span></li>
                            <li class="flex items-center space-x-2"><span class="w-2 h-2 bg-amber-500 rounded-full"></span><span>1 tbsp coriander seeds & 1 tsp cumin seeds</span></li>
                            <li class="flex items-center space-x-2"><span class="w-2 h-2 bg-amber-500 rounded-full"></span><span>3-4 garlic cloves & 1-inch ginger piece</span></li>
                            <li class="flex items-center space-x-2"><span class="w-2 h-2 bg-amber-500 rounded-full"></span><span>2 tablespoons Goda Masala or Kanda Lasun Masala</span></li>
                            <li class="flex items-center space-x-2"><span class="w-2 h-2 bg-amber-500 rounded-full"></span><span>3 tablespoons oil (extra for floating tarri layer)</span></li>
                            <li class="flex items-center space-x-2"><span class="w-2 h-2 bg-amber-500 rounded-full"></span><span>1 tsp mustard seeds, 1 tsp cumin, curry leaves, hing</span></li>
                            <li class="flex items-center space-x-2"><span class="w-2 h-2 bg-amber-500 rounded-full"></span><span>1 tablespoon Kashmiri red chili powder & 2 cups water</span></li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>

                    <div class="space-y-4 pt-4 border-t border-slate-100">
                        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-amber-600">For Assembly & Serving</h3>
                        <ul class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-2 text-slate-700 text-sm">
                            <li class="flex items-center space-x-2"><span class="w-2 h-2 bg-amber-500 rounded-full"></span><span>8 to 10 pav buns</span></li>
                            <li class="flex items-center space-x-2"><span class="w-2 h-2 bg-amber-500 rounded-full"></span><span>Farsan or Chiwda (crispy snack mix)</span></li>
                            <li class="flex items-center space-x-2"><span class="w-2 h-2 bg-amber-500 rounded-full"></span><span>Finely chopped onions and fresh coriander leaves</span></li>
                            <li class="flex items-center space-x-2"><span class="w-2 h-2 bg-amber-500 rounded-full"></span><span>Lemon wedges</span></li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Step-by-Step Instructions with Image -->
            <div id="instructions" class="bg-white p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-slate-100 space-y-6">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 border-b pb-4">Instructions</h2>
                
                <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1563379091339-03b21ab4a4f8?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80" alt="Freshly Prepared Misal Pav" class="w-full h-64 object-cover rounded-xl shadow-inner mb-6">

                <ol class="space-y-6">
                    <li class="flex space-x-4">
                        <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-amber-100 text-amber-800 font-bold rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-sm">1</span>
                        <div>
                            <strong class="block text-slate-900 mb-1">Step 1: Boil the Sprouts</strong>
                            <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">In a pressure cooker, combine sprouted matki, turmeric powder, salt, and 2 cups of water. Cook for 2 to 3 whistles until tender yet holding shape. Set aside.</p>
                        </div>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex space-x-4">
                        <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-amber-100 text-amber-800 font-bold rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-sm">2</span>
                        <div>
                            <strong class="block text-slate-900 mb-1">Step 2: Make the Misal Masala Base</strong>
                            <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Heat 2 tbsp oil in a pan. Sauté sliced onions until golden brown. Add grated coconut, coriander seeds, cumin seeds, ginger, and garlic. Sauté until fragrant, cool, and blend into a smooth paste with water.</p>
                        </div>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex space-x-4">
                        <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-amber-100 text-amber-800 font-bold rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-sm">3</span>
                        <div>
                            <strong class="block text-slate-900 mb-1">Step 3: Prepare the Spicy Rassa (Tarri)</strong>
                            <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Heat 3 tbsp oil in a deep pot. Temper mustard seeds, cumin, curry leaves, and hing. Add ground misal masala paste, sauté until oil separates, then stir in Goda Masala and Kashmiri red chili powder. Add boiled sprouts with cooking water plus 2 extra cups of water and salt. Simmer on low for 15 minutes until a vibrant spicy oil layer (tarri) floats on top.</p>
                        </div>
                    </li>
                    <li class="flex space-x-4">
                        <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-amber-100 text-amber-800 font-bold rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-sm">4</span>
                        <div>
                            <strong class="block text-slate-900 mb-1">Step 4: Assemble and Serve</strong>
                            <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">In a deep bowl, layer cooked sprouts and a handful of crunchy farsan. Ladle piping hot, spicy rassa generously over top. Garnish with chopped raw onions and coriander. Serve with soft pav buns, extra farsan, and lemon wedges. For catered events, coordinate options with professionals like <a href="https://srisaicattering.com" class="text-amber-600 font-medium underline">Sri Sai Catering</a>.</p>
                        </div>
                    </li>
                </ol>
            </div>

        </article>
    </main>

